 2. 🛸 Strange &quot;black triangle&quot; in new UFO docs 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios On a recent evening near a secure U.S. facility, three federal agents say they saw a flying "matte black triangle" that moved as fast as a fighter jet, made no sound and then disappeared, Axios' Marc Caputo writes from new FBI and Defense Department reports. 

 The two reports are included in a batch of documents released today by U.S. officials under President Trump's order to disclose Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena records. 🔺 The agents reported seeing the drone-like triangle, with a wingspan of about 15 feet, rise vertically for as many as 300 feet above a mountain ridgeline without tilting or swaying.

 They say it stopped, hovered for about 20 seconds, then flew horizontally for about 1.5 miles in three seconds without making a sound. Then it simply vanished. ✅ Reality check: The records don't say whether the government believes UAPs are tied to alien life.

