 4. ⚾️ 1 sports thing: Fall Classic begins 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Brewers celebrate a game-winning hit against the San Diego Padres on Oct. 4. Photo: John Fisher/Getty Images The World Series gets underway tonight, with the Tampa Bay Rays taking on the Milwaukee Brewers at 8 p.m. ET.

 The series pits two smaller markets against each other, with both teams reaching baseball's biggest stage despite ranking in the bottom half of MLB payrolls, Axios Tampa Bay's Yacob Reyes writes. 🏆 Milwaukee finished with the league's best record at 103-59. They swept the two-time defending champion Dodgers to reach their first World Series since 1982. 

 Tampa Bay led the American League with 98 wins before beating Cleveland in six games to clinch their third pennant in franchise history. Go deeper ... How to watch . 

 
 
